---
description: Org-wide Spring Boot conventions for EF microservices
globs: src/main/java/**/*
alwaysApply: true
---

# Tech Stack

- Java 17, Spring Boot 3.5.x, Jakarta (`jakarta.*`)
- MongoDB, Artemis/JMS, Redis — for connection patterns, see Infrastructure section
- Reuse external domain libraries; do not redefine shared model types

# Package Layout

- `controller/` — REST (`@RestController`)
- `service/` + `*ServiceImpl` — business logic
- `repository/` — Spring Data Mongo + `*RepositoryImpl` / `*CacheImpl`
- `model/` — Mongo `@Document` entities (`*Entity`)
- `dto/` — REST request/response only
- `config/` — Spring configuration beans
- `exceptions/` — custom exceptions and `@ControllerAdvice` handlers

# Dependency Injection

- Constructor injection only; never field `@Autowired`
- `@Autowired` on constructor is acceptable; implicit constructor injection also used
- Use `ObjectFactory<T>` for prototype-scoped beans where existing code does

# Lombok

- DTOs/entities: `@Getter`, `@Setter`, `@NoArgsConstructor`, `@AllArgsConstructor`, `@ToString`
- GraphQL `types/`: `@Data`, `@Builder` only (if service uses DGS)
- Prefer existing `EfLogger` / `SafeLogger` over introducing new logging styles

# Mapping

- Manual mapping only (Jackson, constructors, utilities)
- Do not introduce MapStruct
